{"name":"Bleached Jade","hex":"#e2e6d1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bleached","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Whitened; made white using bleach","Faded or washed out by weather and strong sunlight."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of bleach"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bleached"},{"term":"jade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A semiprecious stone, either nephrite or jadeite, generally green or white in color, often used for carving figurines.","A bright shade of slightly bluish or greyish green, typical of polished jade stones."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a grayish shade of green, typical of jade stones."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bleached","blocks":[{"text":"Bleached is an American pop band consisting of sisters Jennifer and Jessica Clavin, formerly of Mika Miko. The band plays a style of rock, pop, rock and roll, and indie rock. Bleached was established in Los Angeles in 2011. The group has released three studio albums, Ride Your Heart (2013), Welcome the Worms (2016) and Don't You Think You've Had Enough? (2019), all with Dead Oceans, and have charted on the Billboard charts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Bleached_performing_at_The_Great_Escape%2C_May_2016.jpg/330px-Bleached_performing_at_The_Great_Escape%2C_May_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bleached","wikidata":"Q25056076"},{"title":"Jade","blocks":[{"text":"Jade is an umbrella term for two different types of decorative rocks used for jewelry or ornaments. Jade is often referred to by either of two different silicate mineral names: nephrite, or jadeite. Nephrite is typically green, although it may be yellow, white or black. Jadeite varies from white or near-colorless, through various shades of green, to lavender, yellow, orange, brown and black. Rarely it may be blue. Both of these names refer to their use as gemstones, and each has a mineralogically more specific name. Both the amphibole jade (nephrite) and pyroxene jade are mineral aggregates (rocks) rather than mineral species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Jadestein.jpg/330px-Jadestein.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jade","wikidata":"Q175089"},{"title":"Shades of green","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color green may differ in hue, chroma or lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a green or other hue mixed with white, a shade being mixed with black. A large selection of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Shades_of_Green.svg/330px-Shades_of_Green.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_green","wikidata":"Q19847180"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Bleached_at_Tufnell_Park_Dome%2C_October_2013.jpg/500px-Bleached_at_Tufnell_Park_Dome%2C_October_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Bleached_at_Tufnell_Park_Dome%2C_October_2013.jpg/1280px-Bleached_at_Tufnell_Park_Dome%2C_October_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Bleached_at_Tufnell_Park_Dome%2C_October_2013.jpg/500px-Bleached_at_Tufnell_Park_Dome%2C_October_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bleached performing in London in 2013","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABleached_at_Tufnell_Park_Dome%2C_October_